WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.430
Musa Dagh, the Mountain of Moses,

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.699
rises from the Mediterranean coast
north of the bay of Antioch.

3
00:00:09.739 --> 00:00:12.535
Below it lay six Armenian villages.

4
00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:17.585
In the summer of 1915 they received
the order for deportation,

5
00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:20.667
and they knew what deportation meant.

6
00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:23.082
Most villagers refused to go.

7
00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.992
More than 4,000 people
drove their flocks up the mountain

8
00:00:27.032 --> 00:00:28.534
and dug in.

9
00:00:28.574 --> 00:00:32.004
With Movses Ter-Kalustian
among their leaders,

10
00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:34.244
some 600 fighters blocked the paths

11
00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:37.270
and threw the attackers back
again and again.

12
00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.980
The villagers sewed
two great banners:

13
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.316
a red cross, and the words
'Christians in distress: rescue'.

14
00:00:44.676 --> 00:00:48.927
On 5 September the French cruiser
Guichen saw the signals.

15
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:53.297
Five French ships carried
about 4,000 Armenians to Port Said,

16
00:00:53.337 --> 00:00:56.331
and the mountain
had never been taken.

17
00:00:56.691 --> 00:01:00.024
Hold Musa Dagh until the ships come.

